/-!
# Local coordinates, linear blow-ups, and derivatives of ideals

This file collects local facts used in the resolution of singularities.

* **Coordinate neighbourhoods.** Let `S` be a Noetherian scheme and `0 ∈ S` a closed point whose
  local ring `𝒪_{S,0}` is regular of dimension `2`. If `x, y ∈ 𝒪_S(V)` are sections over an open
  `V ∋ 0` whose germs form a regular system of parameters of `𝒪_{S,0}`, then shrinking `V` to a
  suitable affine open `U ∋ 0` makes `(U, x|_U, y|_U)` a coordinate neighbourhood of `0`.
* **Charts of a linear blow-up.** Let `I ⊆ R[x_σ]` be generated by the coordinates `x_i`,
  `i ∈ s`, for a finite set `s`. The blow-up `π : B_I 𝔸^σ_R → 𝔸^σ_R` is covered by the charts
  `U_j = D_+(x_j)`, `j ∈ s`; each `U_j` is an affine space with coordinates `x_j`,
  `x_i / x_j` (`i ∈ s`, `i ≠ j`) and `x_i` (`i ∉ s`), and `π⁻¹ I` is generated by `x_j` on `U_j`.
* **Smooth blow-up sequences.** In a smooth blow-up sequence `X_r → ⋯ → X_0 = X` starting with a
  smooth scheme over `k` all of whose irreducible components have dimension `n`, every `X_i` is
  smooth with all irreducible components of dimension `n`, their generic points avoid the total
  exceptional set, and inverse images along the blow-ups of ideals nonzero at the generic points
  stay nonzero at the generic points.
* **Derivatives of ideals.** On a smooth scheme over `k` whose irreducible components have
  positive dimension, `I ⊆ D(I)`; in characteristic zero `ord_x D^j(I) = max(ord_x I - j, 0)`, so
  the marked derivatives `D^r(I, m)`, `r < m`, have the cosupport of `(I, m)`, and the support of
  the maximal contact ideal `MC(I) = D^{m-1}(I)` is the cosupport of `(I, maxord I)`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Resolution.CoordinateNeighbourhood.exists_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters`
* `MMP.Resolution.linearBlowUp_charts`
* `MMP.Resolution.ClosedBlowupSequence.IsSmooth.truncate_target_equidimensional`
* `MMP.Resolution.ClosedBlowupSequence.IsSmooth.isNonzeroAtGenericPoints_comap_blowUpToBase`
* `MMP.Resolution.le_higherDerivativeIdeal_and_multAt`
* `MMP.Resolution.MarkedIdeal.cosupport_derivative`
* `MMP.Resolution.support_maximalContactIdeal`

## Implementation notes

* For the coordinate neighbourhood, choose an affine open `0 ∈ W = Spec A ⊆ V` with `𝔪 ⊆ A` the
  prime of `0`. Since `A` is Noetherian there is `g ∉ 𝔪` with `g 𝔪 ⊆ (x, y)` that also kills the
  kernel of `A → A_𝔪`; on `U = D(g)` the ring `A_g` injects into the domain `𝒪_{S,0}` and
  `(x, y) A_g = 𝔪 A_g`. This single shrinking replaces the source's separate shrinkings that
  remove the other minimal primes and the nilradical.
* The chart ring of `D_+(x_j)` is identified with a polynomial ring through the map
  `R[y_σ] → R[x_σ][x_j⁻¹]`, `y_i ↦ x_i / x_j` (`i ∈ s`, `i ≠ j`), `y_i ↦ x_i` otherwise; it is
  injective because, followed by `x_i ↦ y_i y_j`, it is the localization map at the
  nonzerodivisor `y_j`.
* A step `π_i : X_{i+1} → X_i` of a blow-up sequence is written by splitting the sequence as
  `B.append (cons Z C)`, so that `X_i = B.target` and `π_i = blowUpToBase Z`.
* Orders take values in `ℕ∞`, whose truncated subtraction gives `r - j = max(r - j, 0)`.

## References

* [J. Kollár, *Lectures on resolution of singularities*][kollar2007], 1.36, 3.29, 3.47, 3.73,
  3.74, 3.79.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BFM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BFM)
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

